---
import '../styles/site.css';
import deployment from '../../../../docs/deployments/testnet.json';

const repo = 'https://github.com/Sorogate/sorogate';
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="color-scheme" content="light dark" />
    <title>Sorogate policy playground</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Work out an access policy for Stellar in your browser and compare it with the answers the Soroban contract is recorded as giving."
    />
    <link rel="icon" href="data:," />
  </head>
  <body>
    <header>
      <p class="status">
        Early development. Testnet only. Not audited. This page makes no network calls and holds no keys.
      </p>
      <h1>Sorogate policy playground</h1>
      <p>
        An access policy is a short list of conditions about an address: it holds at least some of a token, it holds
        at least some items of a collection, the ledger time is inside a window. All of them must hold. This page works
        a policy out in your browser with the project’s TypeScript model and sets the result beside the answer the
        Soroban contract is recorded as giving for the same input.
      </p>
    </header>

    <main>
      <div id="app">
        <noscript><p class="notice">This page needs JavaScript to work a policy out.</p></noscript>
      </div>

      <section aria-labelledby="deployment-heading">
        <h2 id="deployment-heading">The public Testnet deployment</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>This is a development deployment on Stellar Testnet, not a production deployment.</strong> Testnet is
          reset from time to time, the contract has not been audited, and it has no administrator or upgrade path.
        </p>
        <dl class="facts">
          <dt>Contract</dt>
          <dd><a href={deployment.explorer}><code>{deployment.contract.id}</code></a></dd>
          <dt>WASM hash</dt>
          <dd><code>{deployment.wasm.sha256}</code></dd>
          <dt>Deployed</dt>
          <dd>{deployment.deployedAt.slice(0, 10)}</dd>
        </dl>
        <p>
          How to check that it is the code in this repository, and how it is kept alive:
          <a href={`${repo}/blob/main/docs/DEPLOYMENT.md`}>deployment notes</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="limits-heading">
        <h2 id="limits-heading">What this page cannot tell you</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>The contract decides, not this page.</strong> The model here is a preview and an explanation. It is
            held to the contract by shared test vectors, but only the contract’s own answer counts on the network.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Recorded answers are for the listed examples only.</strong> Change a value and the page says there
            is nothing recorded for that input.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>A policy does not prove who is asking.</strong> The same balance passes for whoever holds it, so a
            contract that acts on a decision must also check that the caller really is that address.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Read the <a href={`${repo}/blob/main/spec/SPEC.md`}>specification</a>, the
          <a href={`${repo}/blob/main/docs/THREAT_MODEL.md`}>threat model</a>, or the <a href={repo}>source</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </main>

    <footer>
      <p>
        Apache-2.0. Not affiliated with or endorsed by the Stellar Development Foundation; “Stellar” and “Soroban” are
        their trademarks.
      </p>
    </footer>

    <script>
      import { examples } from '../playground/examples';
      import { mount } from '../playground/view';

      const app = document.getElementById('app');
      if (app !== null) mount(app, examples);
    </script>
  </body>
</html>
